<title>USA: CCC says wants to redefine sugar crop year.</title>
<headline>CCC says wants to redefine sugar crop year.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Agriculture Department's Commodity Credit Corp proposed Wednesday to redefine the crop year for the sugar loan program to the federal fiscal year, ending Sept 30.</p>
<p>In a notice published in the Federal Register, CCC asked for public comment on its proposal to change the current crop year for the sugar loan program, which runs July 1 through June 30. The proposed rule would extend the loan availability period to the whole fiscal year instead of ending the availability period on June 30.</p>
<p>The proposal would also eliminate an existing restriction that allows CCC to make loans only in July, August, and September on sugar processed from sugarcane or sugar beets that are normally harvested in those months.</p>
<p>CCC asked for public comments by June 2.</p>
<p>((-- Washington commodities desk, 202-898-8300))</p>
